/F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 806 Tm (BIO 201 Genetics, Lecture 7) Tj
/F2 20 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 768 Tm (Genetics and Inheritance) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 733 Tm (These notes cover how traits are passed from parents to offspring, the structure of genes,) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 717.5 Tm (and the experiments that founded modern genetics.) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 689.0 Tm (DNA and Genes) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 666.0 Tm (DNA \(deoxyribonucleic acid\) is the molecule that carries genetic instructions in all living) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 650.5 Tm (organisms. A gene is a segment of DNA that codes for a specific protein. Genes are located) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 635.0 Tm (on chromosomes, which are long strands of DNA wrapped around proteins called histones.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 614.5 Tm (Humans have 23 pairs of chromosomes, for a total of 46. One chromosome of each pair is) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 599.0 Tm (inherited from each parent.) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 570.5 Tm (Alleles) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 547.5 Tm (An allele is a variant form of a gene. A dominant allele is expressed even when only one) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 532.0 Tm (copy is present. A recessive allele is only expressed when two copies are present.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 511.5 Tm (An organism with two identical alleles for a trait is homozygous, while an organism with two) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 496.0 Tm (different alleles is heterozygous. The genotype is the genetic makeup of an organism,) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 480.5 Tm (whereas the phenotype is its set of observable characteristics.) Tj
/F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 280 30 Tm (Page 1 of 3) Tj
