/F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 806 Tm (BIO 201 Genetics, Lecture 7) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 760 Tm (Mendel's Laws) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 737 Tm (Gregor Mendel is known as the father of modern genetics. Mendel performed his experiments on) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 721.5 Tm (pea plants in the 1850s and 1860s.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 701.0 Tm (The law of segregation states that the two alleles for a trait separate during the formation) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 685.5 Tm (of gametes. The law of independent assortment states that genes for different traits are) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 670.0 Tm (inherited independently of each other.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 649.5 Tm (A Punnett square is a diagram used to predict the outcome of a genetic cross. A cross) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 634.0 Tm (between two heterozygous parents produces a 3:1 ratio of dominant to recessive phenotypes.) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 605.5 Tm (Mutations) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 582.5 Tm (A mutation is a permanent change in the DNA sequence. Mutagens are agents, such as) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 567.0 Tm (ultraviolet light and certain chemicals, that increase the rate of mutation.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 546.5 Tm (Types of mutation:) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 68 526.0 Tm (Х Point mutation: a change in a single nucleotide) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 68 509.5 Tm (Х Insertion: one or more nucleotides are added to the sequence) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 68 493.0 Tm (Х Deletion: one or more nucleotides are removed from the sequence) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 68 476.5 Tm (Х Frameshift mutation: an insertion or deletion that shifts the reading frame) Tj
/F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 280 30 Tm (Page 2 of 3) Tj
