/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 760 Tm (Meiosis) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 737 Tm (Meiosis is a type of cell division that produces four genetically different haploid cells.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 721.5 Tm (Gametes are haploid, meaning they contain one set of chromosomes.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 701.0 Tm (Crossing over occurs during prophase I, when homologous chromosomes exchange segments of) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 685.5 Tm (DNA. Crossing over increases genetic variation in the offspring.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 665.0 Tm (Mitosis, by contrast, produces two genetically identical diploid cells and is used for) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 649.5 Tm (growth and repair.) Tj
